# shell-audit-counters

Use when writing or debugging bash under `set -e` that increments counters with `((var++))`/`((n--))` — the arithmetic command returns exit 1 when its result is 0, silently aborting the script on the first increment from zero (and only on bash ≥4, so macOS bash 3.2 hides it until CI).

